                <pb facs="0429" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2308: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-18T20:00:00-04:00">May 18, 1934—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Following cable just received from Gibson at Rio de Janeiro: [Here follows
                    text of telegram No. 89, May 18, 1 p.m., from the Ambassador in Brazil, printed
                    on <ref target="#pg358">page 358</ref>.] You may of course use your
                    discretion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
